  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="370e-a713-fc14-3dad" name="Viking (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>VIKING ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.36-37), 9th-10th century raiders.
Designer's note: a large Anglo-Danish field army is better represented by the Saxon list; early Saxon raiders are better represented by this list (but not Beserkers and Ulfhednar).
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Infantry at least half the points; Archers &amp; Unusual Troops up to a quarter.
Beserkers: a unit of Viking Huscarls can contain up to three Beserkers, represented by ferocious models in the front rank; they may be removed as casualties at the player's choice. If an enemy unit is within 12" of the unit at the start of a Viking turn, roll 2D6 for each Beserker: if the roll is equal to or greater than the distance to the nearest enemy, he charges the closest enemy immediately (automatically if the unit is within 2" of an enemy or in close combat). He causes D6 automatic Strength 5 hits and is then removed from play.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Archers &amp; Unusual Troops: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
